348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 74 0 R
/T (The evidence supports the mechanism. In BIS Working Paper 1270, a USD 3.5bn \(two-standard-deviation\) inflow into dollar-backed stablecoins lowers 3-month T-bill yields by 0.71bps on impact and by up to about 4bps within ten days, with little spillover to longer maturities. The effect roughly doubles to 8 to 10bps when Treasury market intermediaries are under stress, and has grown as the sector has scaled. There is also a geopolitical dimension: dollar tokens can extend demand for US safe assets to users who have never opened a US brokerage account.)
/E (The evidence supports the mechanism. In BIS Working Paper 1270, a USD 3.5bn \(two-standard-deviation\) inflow into dollar-backed stablecoins lowers 3-month T-bill yields by 0.71bps on impact and by up to about 4bps within ten days, with little spillover to longer maturities. The effect roughly doubles to 8 to 10bps when Treasury market intermediaries are under stress, and has grown as the sector has scaled. There is also a geopolitical dimension: dollar tokens can extend demand for US safe assets to users who have never opened a US brokerage account.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
