515 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 78 0 R
/T (The question is no longer whether a token can hold a dollar peg on an exchange. It is who gets to issue private money, what sits behind it, and how these fast-growing private balance sheets interact with public monetary systems. For capital markets, that is the real story.)
/E (The question is no longer whether a token can hold a dollar peg on an exchange. It is who gets to issue private money, what sits behind it, and how these fast-growing private balance sheets interact with public monetary systems. For capital markets, that is the real story.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
