1673 0 obj
<<
/Title (A payment stablecoin is really tokenised private money: built on crypto rails, but only as credible as three things on the issuer's side, its balance sheet, the liquidity of its reserves and the strength of its redemption promise.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1649 0 R
/Prev 1672 0 R
>>
endobj
1674 0 obj
<<
/Title (Transaction volumes have climbed with supply, but for now they are still mostly circling inside the crypto world, above all in settling trades between other digital assets. The real test is whether regulation can push stablecoins past that original niche and into payments, remittances and cross-border settlement. That is where the next section picks up.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1650 0 R
/Next 1675 0 R
>>
