/Title (Crypto-assets run on blockchain infrastructure: transactions are recorded on distributed ledgers, secured cryptographically and verified by network participants rather than a single central authority. That structure makes the market continuous, global and highly liquid, but also fragmented across different chains and prone to fast contagion when confidence breaks.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1670 0 R
/Next 1689 0 R
>>
endobj
1689 0 obj
<<
/Title (Stablecoins sit inside this ecosystem but do a different job from speculative assets like Bitcoin or Ether, whose prices move with supply and demand. A stablecoin is built to hold a steady value against a reference asset, usually the US dollar. Issuers defend that peg in three broad ways.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1670 0 R
/Prev 1688 0 R
/First 1698 0 R
/Last 1699 0 R
/Count -2
>>
endobj
